# Agastya Healthcare — Web Bluetooth API Integration Rules

## Project Context

**Domain:** agastyahealthcare.com  
**Stack:** JWT-authenticated web app with patient/doctor dashboards, Agora video calls, AI chat  
**Bluetooth Scope:** BLE 4.0+ medical devices — spirometers, pulse oximeters, BP monitors, glucometers  
**Target Users:** Chrome on Desktop (Windows/macOS/Linux) and Chrome on Android  
**Not Supported:** Safari (iOS/macOS), Firefox — handle gracefully with fallback UI  

---

## 1. Browser & Environment Checks

Always gate every Bluetooth feature behind a capability check. Never call `navigator.bluetooth` without checking first.

```typescript
// lib/bluetooth/bluetoothSupport.ts

export function isWebBluetoothSupported(): boolean {
  return (
    typeof navigator !== "undefined" &&
    "bluetooth" in navigator &&
    window.isSecureContext // Must be HTTPS or localhost
  );
}

export function getBluetoothUnsupportedReason(): string {
  if (typeof navigator === "undefined") return "Not running in browser";
  if (!window.isSecureContext)
    return "Web Bluetooth requires HTTPS. Please access via agastyahealthcare.com";
  if (!("bluetooth" in navigator)) {
    const ua = navigator.userAgent;
    if (/iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(ua))
      return "Web Bluetooth is not supported on iOS Safari. Please use an Android device or desktop Chrome.";
    if (/Firefox/.test(ua))
      return "Web Bluetooth is not supported in Firefox. Please use Chrome or Edge.";
    if (/Safari/.test(ua) && !/Chrome/.test(ua))
      return "Web Bluetooth is not supported in Safari. Please use Chrome or Edge.";
    return "Web Bluetooth is not supported in your browser. Please use Chrome 56+ or Edge 79+.";
  }
  return "";
}
```

